itted on the current branch as `refactor(common): migrate constants.js to TypeScript`. All three acceptance commands pass:\n- **Type check** (`npx tsc`): no errors.\n- **Unit tests** (`unit.sh`): 14 suites, 554 passed, 1 skipped.\n- **Lint** (`lint:check`): 0 errors. There is 1 warning, and it is in `AdminPanel/.../useAiPlugin.js`, which this packet doesn't touch.\n\n**What I did**\n- Renamed `Common/sources/constants.js` to `constants.ts` with `git mv`, so git records it as a rename and the old `.js` is no longer tracked.\n- In the `.ts`, I added `as const` to the six object and array literals: `RIGHTS`, `LICENSE_MODE`, `LICENSE_RESULT`, `TEMPLATES_FOLDER_LOCALE_COLLISON_MAP`, `TABLE_RESULT_SCHEMA` and `TABLE_CHANGES_SCHEMA`. I also added the house-style header comment. All names, values and their order are unchanged, and the build regenerates `constants.js` from it.\n- Added one `Common/sources/constants.js` line to both `.gitignore` and `.prettierignore`, next to the `utilsDocService.js` line.\n- Diff: 3 files, +13/−6.\n\n**Decisions**\n- I kept the `exports.NAME = ...` assignments exactly as they were, without wrapping the values in a typed object. This keeps the diff minimal and the exported object byte-for-byte the same. The downside is that `exports` is typed as `any` in Node's type definitions, so the `as const` types don't reach other files. This file gets literal types inside it, but no checked interface for the modules that use it.\n- `as const` is a type-only annotation and is removed at build time. So making the arrays read-only in the types does not change any runtime behaviour, including for callers that might change those arrays.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas**\n- In a CommonJS `.ts` file, `exports.X = ...` type-checks without errors because `exports` is `any`. That is easy to migrate, but it gives callers no type safety. Getting real types for callers needs a typed export pattern, for example declaring `const X = ... as const` and then `module.exports.X = X`. That pattern should be settled in a later packet.\n- Pure-data leaf modules like this one are the cheapest migrations: no `require`s and no external input.\n\nPer the run rules I didn't edit anything under `.theseus/queue/` or append to `friction.jsonl`, so the packet's executor log and Atlas lessons sections are still empty. The notes above would need to go there.","ttft_ms":2106,"type":"result","duration_ms":59212,"uuid":"9f4af24f-6f07-4053-95e9-3ec2c9a30045","ttft_stream_ms":1029,"time_to_request_ms":484,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":10,"system_prompt":235,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":6,"input_attachments":41,"input_hooks":4,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":15,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":29,"init_frame_send":10,"engine_pickup":12,"loop_entry":6,"message_prep":2,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":3,"request_announcements":18,"query_setup":5,"auto_mode_context_wait":20,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":35,"message_normalization":4,"client_creation":12,"request_build":14},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":134,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":351,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":216,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":140,"process_rss_mib_result":238,"process_anon_mib_result":146,"process_peak_rss_mib":238,"process_cpu_ms_turn":2572,"process_wall_ms_turn":59212,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1348,"process_wall_ms_streaming":31233,"main_stream_count":10,"main_stream_event_count":662,"main_stream_chunk_count":383,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":19,"cpu_ms":41,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":1,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":17,"ambient_wait_ms":18,"render_ms":3,"producers":41,"token_counts":0},"first_content_frame_ms":1029,"time_to_request_from_spawn_ms":3584143,"warm_spare_claimed":false,"flag_fetch_kick":"started_in_init_warm","time_origin_ms":1793623342077.678,"queued_turn_count":0,"resu